<%#
  A status pill: one word or one number, read at a glance beside the thing it
  describes (docs/design/GUIDELINES.md section 3, "Badge").

  Locals:
    label:   the text — an outcome ("denied"), a count ("7"). Keep it to a word.
    variant: :ok (the call did what was asked), :denied (refused or failed) or
             :neutral (a plain fact with no verdict, e.g. a counter). Defaults
             to :neutral.
    id:      the element id, if tests or links hold on to it
    class:   extra classes for the pill, usually spacing

  Border plus fill in one family, like shared/_alert, so the three variants are
  one box in three colours rather than three differently sized pills — and so
  danger-tint never appears without its danger border (section 1).

  The colour is decoration: it repeats what the label already says, so nothing
  here is announced separately and a screen reader hears the word on its own.
%>
<% variant = local_assigns.fetch(:variant, :neutral).to_sym %>
<%= tag.span id: local_assigns[:id],
      class: [ "inline-flex items-center rounded-full border px-2.5 py-0.5 text-[13px] font-semibold",
               { ok: "border-green bg-green-tint text-green-deep",
                 denied: "border-danger bg-danger-tint text-danger-deep",
                 neutral: "border-line bg-surface-hover text-ink-soft" }.fetch(variant),
               local_assigns[:class] ] do %><%= label %><% end %>
